+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool registers a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that providers already receive verbatim, yet `ToolRegistry.execute` historically forwarded model inputs to executors without checking them. This specification defines the validation boundary inside `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` so malformed tool arguments fail predictably as a `ToolResponse` the model can recover from inside `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts`.
+
+## Input validation contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates input against the resolved `inputSchema` before calling the executor, returning a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing property path and constraint while calling the executor zero times and leaking no input values into results or logs ([validated by: rejects invalid input with path and constraint, calls executor zero times, and leaks no values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L17)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared types, and `enum` only, forwarding valid input with unlisted properties unmodified without injecting defaults or coercing types ([validated by: forwards valid input with extra properties unmodified without defaults or coercion](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L84)).
+- Static tool definitions compile their `inputSchema` once at `register` time—throwing an error naming the tool on an uncompilable schema—while `execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` for unregistered tool names ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration, rejects broken schemas, and throws on unknown tools](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L122)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition per `execute` call and validates against the schema current at that call ([validated by: validates a function-valued tool definition against the schema current at each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L166)).
+- Function-valued tool definitions returning the same schema object reference across calls reuse the cached compiled validator rather than recompiling it.
+- Inside the orchestrator tool loop, a schema-rejected tool call returns its `ToolResponse` as a `tool_result` message so the model can retry within the round budget without triggering `onError` ([validated by: feeds schema rejection back to the provider and resolves after retry](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L17)).
